  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p style=\"text-align: justify; \"><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\"><u><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Enlargement of a dwelling house (Class A)</span></u><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"> - The operations,&nbsp;</span></span>comprising the replacement of an existing garage door with a domestic window, would consist of the enlargement of a dwelling house\r\nwithin the meaning of Class A of Part 1 of Schedule 2 to the Town &amp; Country\r\nPlanning (General Permitted Development)&nbsp;\r\n(England) Order 2015 \"the Order\" and would comply with the\r\ndevelopment tolerances set out in said Class A. The operation would therefore\r\nhave been granted planning permission by Article 3 of the Order.</p>",
    "<p><span style=\"line-height: 107%;\"><u>Not development</u> - The works do not constitute development as defined in Section 55 of the\r\nTown & Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended). Therefore no planning\r\npermission would be required.</span></p>"
